# Flash lets the Armor arrive after blockers are declared. Bot1 attacks with Elvish Mystic and Bot2's Ornithopter (0/2 flier) blocks it;
# Bot1 then flashes in Celestial Armor onto the Mystic, which becomes a 3/1 flier with hexproof and indestructible. Giving it flying
# after blockers does not remove the block (CR 509.1h): the Mystic stays blocked, deals its 3 damage to the Ornithopter (dies) and none to
# Bot2, who stays at 20. The Ornithopter deals 0, so the Mystic survives with no damage (it is indestructible anyway).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Elvish Mystic
Celestial Armor
Island
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Plains x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Elvish Mystic.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Elvish Mystic > Bot2)
Bot2.Block(Ornithopter > Elvish Mystic)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Celestial Armor.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Combat.Blocks = Ornithopter > Elvish Mystic
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter
Bot1.Battlefield.Celestial Armor.AttachedTo = Elvish Mystic
Bot1.Battlefield.Elvish Mystic.Damage = 0
